WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.900
The second CTE parses dates It recognizes two
documented

00:00:05.927 --> 00:00:11.755
formats If the raw text matches one of them
PostgreSQL creates

00:00:11.768 --> 00:00:17.338
a typed date If the value does not match a supported
format the clean

00:00:17.364 --> 00:00:23.275
date becomes NULL That preserves the distinction
between known and unsupported

00:00:23.301 --> 00:00:23.788
input
